          "2": "½ tsp",
          "3": "½ tsp",
          "4": "½ tsp"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "step-2",
      "number": 2,
      "heading": "Roast the chicken",
      "blocks": [
        "Transfer the chicken to a baking tray, skin-side up. Sprinkle half the Mediterranean style seasoning over it.",
        "Roast on the top shelf for 12–15 minutes, until cooked through and no longer pink in the middle."
      ],
      "notes": [],
      "timers": [
        {
          "id": "timer-1",
          "label": "Roast chicken",
          "seconds": [
            720,
            900
          ]
        }
      ],
      "image": {
        "id": "pesto-orzo-2",
        "path": "media/pesto-orzo-2-sketch.webp",
        "width": 640,
        "height": 480,
        "alt": "Sketch of two browned chicken breasts spaced apart on a rectangular baking tray",
        "credit": "Illustration based on the HelloFresh recipe card"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "step-3",
      "number": 3,
      "heading": "Cook the veg",
      "blocks": [
        "While the chicken fries, remove the root and dark leaves of the leek. Halve it lengthways and slice thinly.",
        "Trim the carrot, quarter lengthways without peeling and chop it across into small pieces. Trim and thinly slice the spring onion.",
        "While the chicken roasts, put the same frying pan over medium-high heat with a drizzle of oil. Stir-fry the carrot and leek for 6–8 minutes until tender."
      ],
      "notes": [],
      "timers": [
        {
          "id": "timer-1",
          "label": "Soften vegetables",
          "seconds": [
            360,
            480
          ]
        }
      ],
      "image": {
        "id": "pesto-orzo-3",
        "path": "media/pesto-orzo-3-sketch.webp",
        "width": 640,
        "height": 480,
        "alt": "Sketch of finely chopped orange carrot and green leek in the frying pan",
        "credit": "Illustration based on the HelloFresh recipe card"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "step-4",
      "number": 4,
      "heading": "Boil the orzo",
      "blocks": [
        "While the vegetables cook, add orzo to the boiling water and bring it back to a boil. Cook for 10 minutes until tender.",
        "Drain in a sieve, return to the saucepan and stir through a little oil to prevent sticking."
      ],
      "notes": [],
      "timers": [
        {
          "id": "timer-1",
          "label": "Boil orzo",
          "seconds": [
            600
          ]
        }
      ],
      "image": {
        "id": "pesto-orzo-4",
        "path": "media/pesto-orzo-4-sketch.webp",
        "width": 640,
        "height": 480,
        "alt": "Sketch of two-handled saucepan full of plain cooked orzo",
        "credit": "Illustration based on the HelloFresh recipe card"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "step-5",
      "number": 5,
      "heading": "Finish the orzo",
      "blocks": [
        "When the vegetables are tender, stir in {{line-6}} chicken stock paste, {{line-7}} crème fraîche, {{line-11}} water and the remaining seasoning.",
        "Simmer for 2–3 minutes, then take off the heat. Stir in the pesto and cooked orzo to coat.",
        "If the sauce is thick, loosen with a splash of water. Season to taste."
      ],
      "notes": [],
      "timers": [
        {
          "id": "timer-1",
          "label": "Simmer the sauce",
          "seconds": [
            120,
            180
          ]
        }
      ],
